      "descriptor": "Bomber-style build shown unworn and laid flat: the diamond quilt channels run on a wide diagonal grid across the whole body front and stop at the shoulder/armhole line, while the sleeves are plain unquilted shell from the armhole seam down, so the quilted torso and smooth sleeves read as two distinct panel zones. The knit trims are a single contrasting sand-toned rib used three times — a low stand band at the neck, deep bands at both sleeve ends, and a hem band that is interrupted at centre front where the zipper tape passes through it, leaving the black hem facing exposed in a narrow strip on either side of the zip. Zip runs edge-to-edge from that hem interruption up to the top of the neck band with a small dark pull at the head. A short horizontal welt opening sits low on each front panel, sunk into the quilting and barely legible against it. Inner neck shows a small dark woven label on a black facing; the collar folds slightly open so the inside of the neck band is visible.",
